        "description": "<div style='text-align:center;'><i><span style='font-weight:bold;'>To protect human health and the </span></i><i><span style='font-weight:bold;'>quality of Idaho’s air, land, and water.</span></i><br /></div><i><br /></i>\n<p>DEQ is a state department created by the Idaho Environmental \nProtection and Health Act to ensure clean air, water, and land in the \nstate and protect Idaho citizens from the adverse health impacts of \npollution.</p>\n<p>As a regulatory agency, DEQ enforces various state environmental \nregulations and administers a number of federal environmental protection\n laws including the Clean Air Act, the Clean Water Act, and the Resource\n Conservation and Recovery Act.</p>\n<p>The agency is committed to working in partnership with local \ncommunities, businesses, and citizens to identify and implement \ncost-effective environmental solutions.</p>",
